{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1723","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1723","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1723\",\"parent_revision\":\"3a053de5e73a15450cf0af1c8906d3ea354058db\",\"root_revision\":\"53d0268a22c0b363d1948c162159eed09e0e665fddd31de0405f17f53baa55eb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claims verified (2026-04-19):**\\n\\n**Claim 1**: `artifact_read` at server.py:2580-2583 has only `issue_number` and `artifact_type` parameters\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: No offset, limit, or page parameters exist in artifact_read\\n- evidence: File read \u2014 server.py:2580-2583: `async def artifact_read(issue_number: ..., artifact_type: ...)` \u2014 exactly two parameters\\n- source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2580-2583\\n\\n**Claim 2**: `ArtifactContent` model at models.py:1371-1388 has only artifact_type, path, content, status fields\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: ArtifactContent has no pagination fields (total_lines, has_more, offset, limit)\\n- evidence: File read \u2014 models.py:1371-1388: four fields only (artifact_type, path, content, status)\\n- source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py:1371-1388\\n\\n**Claim 3**: All four provider `read_artifact_content` implementations lack offset/limit parameters\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: GistProvider at :531, GitHub at :479, GitLab at :868, Linear at :1091 all return full string with no range arguments\\n- evidence: Bash grep \u2014 artifact_provider.py shows `def read_artifact_content(self, path: str)` and `def read_artifact_content_from_remote(self, issue_number: int, artifact_type: str, path: str)` at all four providers with no offset/limit\\n- source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py:270,310,327,479,531,562\\n\\n**Claim 4**: `backlog_view` already supports offset/limit pagination\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: backlog_view has established offset/limit entry-block pagination at server.py:1725-1726\\n- evidence: Bash grep \u2014 backlog_view signature in server.py references offset and limit pagination parameters (per item description citing server.py:1726-1727)\\n- source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1725-1727\\n\\n**Claim 5**: Multiple SAM pipeline skills/agents call artifact_read\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: planning, implement-feature, final-verification, context-integration, complete-implementation, add-new-feature, work-backlog-item, feature-verifier, plan-validator, swarm-task-planner, t0-baseline-capture all call artifact_read\\n- evidence: Bash grep for 'artifact_read' in skills/ and agents/ returned matches in all listed files\\n- source: plugins/development-harness/skills/ and agents/ (grep 2026-04-19)\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: feat: artifact_read cannot stream large artifacts within the 10K-token MCP call ceiling\\nDate: 2026-04-19\\nGoal: Add offset/limit pagination to artifact_read so callers can window large artifact content within the MCP token ceiling.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description: add offset/limit line-range params to artifact_read\\n2. Scope boundaries | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File read \u2014 server.py:2580-2583, models.py:ArtifactContent, artifact_provider.py provider hierarchy confirmed\\n3. External interfaces | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File read \u2014 MCP tool contract at server.py:2580; four provider implementations at artifact_provider.py:270,479,531,868,1091\\n4. Constraints | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User instructions \u2014 no cast()/object/Any; TypedDict or Pydantic for structured data; backward-compatible defaults required\\n5. Existing system context | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File read \u2014 four provider implementations confirmed; backlog_view offset/limit pattern at server.py:1726-1727 confirmed as model\\n6. Verification expectations | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Bash glob \u2014 test_artifact_content_storage.py and test_artifact_provider.py exist and cover artifact_read\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- All 6 conditions confirmed AVAILABLE via tool verification on 2026-04-19\\n- No conditions regressed; no new conditions discovered\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **artifact_read cannot stream large artifacts within the 10k-token mcp call ceiling** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Verified code audit 2026-04-12 \u2014 backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification.md (u3) + round2 (Q2)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-12\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-13)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Call `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")` on an issue whose artifact file exceeds ~10,000 tokens.\\n2. Observe the MCP response: the full `content` field is returned as a single string with no pagination metadata.\\n3. The caller has no `offset`, `limit`, or `total_lines`/`total_chars` field to use for a follow-up call.\\n4. If the artifact exceeds the MCP ceiling the response is truncated or the call is rejected \u2014 there is no page-2 call path.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- `server.py:2580-2583`: `artifact_read` signature has only `issue_number` and `artifact_type` \u2014 no offset, limit, or page parameters.\\n- `models.py:1371-1388`: `ArtifactContent` model has `artifact_type`, `path`, `content`, `status` \u2014 no `total_lines`, `total_chars`, `offset`, `limit`, or `has_more`.\\n- `artifact_provider.py:531-560` (GistProvider), `479-505` (GitHub), `868-887` (GitLab), `1117-1136` (Linear): all four `read_artifact_content` implementations return the full string with no range arguments.\\n- `artifact_provider.py:562-589`: `read_local_artifact_content` returns `str | None` with no range arguments.\\n- Evidence files: `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification.md` \u00a7u3 and round2 \u00a7Q2.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Every SAM pipeline skill and agent that calls `artifact_read` is blocked from reading large artifacts (architecture specs, codebase analyses) through the MCP surface. Worktree-isolated agents have no filesystem fallback and are fully broken for large artifacts.\\nEffort: Medium \u2014 four provider read_artifact_content implementations, ArtifactContent model (5 new fields), tool wrapper (2 new params), new tests for windowed reads; all backward-compatible\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: every SAM pipeline stage that reads a plan artifact exceeding the MCP ceiling \u2014 S2 planning, S3 context integration, S5 implementation, S6 forensic review, S7 final verification.\\n- Bottleneck: worktree-isolated agents (spawned by `/work-milestone`) have no filesystem fallback; they depend exclusively on `artifact_read` and are fully broken for large artifacts.\\n- Inconsistency: `backlog_view` already supports `offset`/`limit` entry-block pagination (server.py:1726-1727); `artifact_read` is the only content-reading tool without it.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Any artifact of any size can be read through the MCP surface without hitting the ceiling.\\n- Worktree-isolated agents gain reliable access to large plan artifacts.\\n- Consistent pagination API across all content-reading MCP tools (`backlog_view`, `artifact_read`).\\n- Callers can implement progressive disclosure (metadata first via `artifact_get`, then windowed content via `artifact_read` with offset/limit).\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `artifact_read` is called with `offset=0, limit=0` (defaults), the current full-content response is returned unchanged. When called with `offset=N, limit=M`, only lines N through N+M-1 of the content are returned, with `total_lines` and `has_more` in the response so the caller can plan subsequent calls. Slicing happens inside the tool before the response is serialized \u2014 the MCP framework never sees the full content when only a window is requested.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe target state is observable through MCP tool calls:\\n\\n- `artifact_read` accepts `offset: int = 0` and `limit: int = 0` parameters (line-based, `limit=0` means no truncation).\\n- The response includes `total_lines: int`, `total_chars: int`, `offset: int`, `limit: int`, and `has_more: bool` alongside the existing `content`, `artifact_type`, `path`, and `status` fields.\\n- `ArtifactContent` Pydantic model in `models.py` is extended with the five new fields (all with defaults so existing `model_dump` callers are unaffected).\\n- The four provider `read_artifact_content` implementations and `read_artifact_content_from_remote` in `GistProvider` accept optional `offset`/`limit` parameters; slicing is applied before return so callers never receive the full string when a window is requested. This keeps the slicing logic at the provider boundary, not in the tool wrapper.\\n- `read_local_artifact_content` in `GistProvider` (artifact_provider.py:562-589) accepts the same optional parameters.\\n- No `cast()`, `object`, or `Any` types introduced. All new parameters and return structures use concrete types or Pydantic `BaseModel` fields.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type=T)` called with no `offset`/`limit` returns the full `content` as today \u2014 backward-compatible default confirmed by running existing tests green: `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_artifact_content_storage.py -k artifact_read -x`.\\n2. `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type=T, offset=0, limit=50)` returns at most 50 lines in `content`, sets `total_lines >= 50`, `has_more=True` when the artifact has more than 50 lines \u2014 verified by a new test in `test_artifact_content_storage.py`.\\n3. `artifact_read(..., offset=50, limit=50)` returns lines 50-99, sets `offset=50`, `limit=50`, `has_more` based on remaining lines \u2014 verified by a new test.\\n4. `artifact_read(..., offset=<beyond_end>, limit=50)` returns `content=\\\"\\\"`, `has_more=False` \u2014 verified by a new test.\\n5. `ArtifactContent.model_dump(mode=\\\"json\\\")` output includes `total_lines`, `total_chars`, `offset`, `limit`, `has_more` \u2014 verified by `uv run pytest` on a unit test for the model.\\n6. `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/` exits 0 with no new errors (no `cast()`, `object`, or `Any` types introduced).\\n7. `uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/` exits 0.\\n8. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_artifact_content_storage.py plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py -x` exits 0.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work (pattern) | `server.py:1726-1727` \u2014 `backlog_view` offset/limit pagination model |\\n| Prior work (model) | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py:1371-1388` \u2014 `ArtifactContent` Pydantic model |\\n| Prior work (tests) | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_artifact_content_storage.py:604-700` \u2014 existing artifact_read test suite |\\n| Prior work (tests) | `plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py:1025-1121` \u2014 integration tests for artifact_read |\\n| Prior work (provider) | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` \u2014 four provider implementations |\\n| Skill | /dh:development-harness |\\n| Agent | @dh:backlog-item-groomer |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 self-contained change in `backlog_core/`.\\n- Blocks: #1728 (MCP tool descriptions do not document ceiling) \u2014 that item should be updated after this change adds pagination to `artifact_read`.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone \u2014 all inputs AVAILABLE. No external dependencies. No missing research.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Four provider implementations (`GitHubGistArtifactProvider`, `GitHubArtifactProvider`, `GitLabArtifactProvider`, `LinearArtifactProvider`) and one Protocol (`ArtifactProviderProtocol`) each need `offset`/`limit` added to `read_artifact_content`. The `ArtifactContent` model gains five fields. The `artifact_read` tool wrapper gains two parameters and must pass them through to the provider call. New tests cover windowed reads, beyond-end offset, and default behavior. No schema migration required. No external API changes (Gist/GitLab APIs return full content; slicing happens post-fetch at the provider layer).\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- Multiple agent/skill files listed under Consumers above \u2014 no immediate instruction changes required (pagination is additive; existing call patterns work unchanged via backward-compatible defaults)\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/planning/SKILL.md` \u2014 calls `artifact_read` for feature-context; benefits from pagination when feature-context exceeds ceiling\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 calls `artifact_read` for architect spec; most commonly large artifact\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/final-verification/SKILL.md` \u2014 calls `artifact_read` for feature-context and architect\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/context-integration/SKILL.md` \u2014 calls `artifact_read` for architect\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 calls `artifact_read` for TN-verification and codebase-analysis\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 calls `artifact_read` for prior artifacts\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/analyze.md` \u2014 calls `artifact_read` for feature-context\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` \u2014 calls `artifact_read` for architect and task-plan\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md` \u2014 calls `artifact_read` for architect and feature-context\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 calls `artifact_read` for T0-baseline and TN-verification\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/t0-baseline-capture.md` \u2014 reads artifacts via artifact_read\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_artifact_content_storage.py:604-700` \u2014 existing artifact_read test suite; backward-compat tests must stay green; new windowed-read tests added\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py:1025-1121` \u2014 provider integration tests; must cover new offset/limit signatures\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::artifact_read` (line 2580) \u2014 gains `offset: int = 0` and `limit: int = 0` parameters; response dict gains `total_lines`, `total_chars`, `has_more` fields\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py::ArtifactContent` (line 1371) \u2014 gains five new Pydantic fields with defaults; backward-compatible\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` \u2014 all four provider `read_artifact_content` implementations gain optional `offset`/`limit`; `ArtifactProviderProtocol.read_artifact_content` signature updated\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: ALIGNED\\n**Rationale**: CLAUDE.md \u00a7'No Invented Limits' states: \\\"When pagination is needed, provide `--offset`/`--limit` parameters (like the `Read` tool) so the caller controls the window.\\\" This change implements exactly that rule for `artifact_read`. The `backlog_view` tool already follows this pattern (server.py:1726-1727) \u2014 making `artifact_read` consistent with `backlog_view` closes a design inconsistency explicitly documented in the item description.\\n**Citations**:\\n- Design rule: `.claude/CLAUDE.md` \u00a7'No Invented Limits' \u2014 \\\"provide `--offset`/`--limit` parameters\\\"\\n- Established pattern: `server.py:1726-1727` \u2014 `backlog_view` offset/limit pagination (the model to follow)\\n- Item description: \\\"Existing `backlog_view` already supports `offset`/`limit` entry-block pagination \u2014 `artifact_read` is the only content-reading tool without it\\\"\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- MCP tool docstring at `server.py:2584-2601` \u2014 needs `offset`/`limit` parameter documentation\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` \u2014 artifact_read tool description should note pagination\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: unbounded-design\\n**Rationale**: The `artifact_read` tool was designed to retrieve artifact content but the design did not account for the MCP response token ceiling (~10,000 tokens). No upper bound is enforced on the returned content size, and no pagination mechanism exists. This is a design scope problem \u2014 the tool was not designed to handle arbitrary-size artifacts within a bounded channel.\\n**Analysis Method**: design-framing\\n**Scenario Target**: Agent calls `artifact_read` on a large architecture spec or codebase analysis artifact \u2192 response truncated or rejected at MCP ceiling \u2192 agent cannot access its own prior output \u2192 add offset/limit pagination following the established `backlog_view` pattern\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `backlog_core/server.py::artifact_read` \u2014 MCP tool layer; gains offset/limit params\\n- `backlog_core/models.py::ArtifactContent` \u2014 response model; gains pagination fields\\n- `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` \u2014 provider protocol + four implementations; gain optional offset/limit at read boundary\\n- 11+ skills and agents that call artifact_read (consumers; backward-compatible; no immediate changes needed)\\n- Test files at test_artifact_content_storage.py and test_artifact_provider.py \u2014 receive new pagination tests\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification.md` \u00a7u3\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification-round2.md` \u00a7Q2\\n- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` \u2192 \\\"No Invented Limits\\\" (the MCP 10K ceiling is external, so the tool must provide pagination)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Agents that register large artifacts (typical for codebase analysis or design specs) cannot read their own output back through the MCP surface once it exceeds the call ceiling.\\n- The consumer is forced to shell out to `gh api` or read the local file directly, bypassing the artifact abstraction.\\n- Existing `backlog_view` already supports `offset`/`limit` entry-block pagination (server.py:1725-1726) \u2014 the artifact read path is inconsistent with that established pattern.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2579-2629` defines `artifact_read` with exactly two parameters \u2014 `issue_number` and `artifact_type`. There is no `offset`, `limit`, or `page`. The function returns the complete artifact content as one `content` field.\\n\\nDownstream, `read_artifact_content_from_remote` (`artifact_provider.py:531-575`) returns `gist_file.content` as a single string with no range support, and `read_local_artifact_content` returns the whole file or `None`. Neither function accepts byte-range or line-range arguments.\\n\\nA single MCP tool call is capped at ~10,000 tokens of response. Artifacts that exceed that ceiling \u2014 architecture specs, codebase analyses, long plans \u2014 cannot be read via `artifact_read` at all. The caller has no way to fetch page 2, a byte range, or a line window.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3a05a454ac95b1540ecaa0ba4682d0559a439951113319ccac151a9fbf3788a2\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnI_vA\"}"}